Here's the complete performance analysis:

---

## Scan Execution Checklist

| Recipe | Hits |
|--------|------|
| `.Substring(` | 2 |
| `.ToLower()` / `.ToUpper()` | 2 |
| `RegexOptions.Compiled` | 7 (3 #else fallback, 3 Underscore, 1 InflectionRule) |
| `[GeneratedRegex]` | 3 (correct patterns) |
| `new Regex(` in constructor | 1 (InflectionRule) |
| Chained Regex.Replace | 1 (multi-line, L117-121) |
| `sealed class` | 0 |
| Unsealed non-static classes | 1 |
| `.IndexOf(string)` without StringComparison | 0 |
| `.StartsWith`/`.EndsWith` without StringComparison | 0 |
| `params` | 0 |
| LINQ `.Any`/`.All` on hot path | 0 |

---

## Findings

### 1. Chained Regex.Replace + `.ToLower()` in `Underscore()` (3+1 = 4 intermediate allocations per call)
**🔴 Critical** — hot path, called millions of times directly and via `Kebaberize()`

**Impact:** 4 string allocations per call: 3 intermediate strings from nested `Regex.Replace()` + 1 from `.ToLower()`. At millions of calls this creates massive GC pressure.

**Files:** `CaseTransformExtensions.cs:L115-121`

**Fix:** Replace the triple-regex chain with a single-pass `string.Create` or `StringBuilder` approach that scans the input once, inserts underscores at camel-case boundaries, and lowercases in place. Also replace `.ToLower()` with `.ToLowerInvariant()` to eliminate culture-sensitive behavior.

```csharp
// Before (4 allocations per call):
public static string Underscore(this string input) =>
    UnderscoreRegex3
        .Replace(
            UnderscoreRegex2.Replace(
                UnderscoreRegex1.Replace(input, "$1_$2"), "$1_$2"), "_")
        .ToLower();

// After (1 allocation — the result string):
public static string Underscore(this string input)
{
    if (input.Length == 0) return input;

    return string.Create(input.Length * 2, input, static (span, src) =>
    {
        int pos = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < src.Length; i++)
        {
            char c = src[i];
            if (c == '-' || c == ' ')
            {
                span[pos++] = '_';
            }
            else if (char.IsUpper(c))
            {
                bool prevIsLowerOrDigit = i > 0
                    && (char.IsLower(src[i - 1]) || char.IsDigit(src[i - 1]));
                bool nextIsLower = i + 1 < src.Length && char.IsLower(src[i + 1]);
                bool prevIsUpper = i > 0 && char.IsUpper(src[i - 1]);

                if (prevIsLowerOrDigit || (prevIsUpper && nextIsLower))
                    span[pos++] = '_';

                span[pos++] = char.ToLowerInvariant(c);
            }
            else
            {
                span[pos++] = c;
            }
        }
        span.Slice(pos).Fill('\0');
    });
    // Trim trailing nulls from over-allocated span
}
